<title>UK: Downgrade of Swedish sovereign debt unlikely-S &amp; P.</title>
<headline>Downgrade of Swedish sovereign debt unlikely-S &amp; P.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A downgrade of Sweden's sovereign debt rating is now less likely, according to Konrad Reuss, a director at Standard and Poor's rating agency in London.</p>
<p>&quot;The likelihood of a downgrade is more and more unlikely, with the economic improvements we have seen receently in Sweden,&quot; Reuss told Reuters before a conference in London.  </p>
<p>S &amp; P currently rates Sweden's sovereign debt at AA+ long-term, with a negative outlook.</p>
<p>Reuss said the negative outlook was still a key signal about Sweden's debt for financial markets.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still just as important because we cannot rule out the possibility of slippage (in the fiscal situation),&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
